CREATE FUNCTION normalise_order() RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$
BEGIN
    NEW.status := lower(NEW.status);
END;
$$;
CREATE TRIGGER orders_norm BEFORE INSERT ON orders
FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION normalise_order();

questions.answer:
A trigger function must end with a RETURN. A BEFORE ROW trigger must `RETURN NEW` (returning NULL would silently skip the row). Add `RETURN NEW;`.
```sql
BEGIN
    NEW.status := lower(NEW.status);
    RETURN NEW;
END;
```
